   "source": [
    "best_bm25 = pt.BatchRetrieve(\n",
    "    index,\n",
    "    wmodel=\"BM25\",\n",
    "    num_results=5000,\n",
    "    controls={\"bm25.k_1\": 0.9, \"bm25.b\": 0.75}\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "bm25_val_candidates = best_bm25.transform(val_queries_pt)\n",
    "\n",
    "bm25_val_candidates = bm25_val_candidates.rename(columns={\n",
    "    \"qid\": \"query_id\",\n",
    "    \"docno\": \"doc_id\"\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "bm25_val_candidates[\"query_id\"] = bm25_val_candidates[\"query_id\"].astype(str)\n",
    "bm25_val_candidates[\"doc_id\"] = bm25_val_candidates[\"doc_id\"].astype(str)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "Hr9mAqRjmM4Z",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "Hr9mAqRjmM4Z"
   },
   "source": [
    " The best-performing configuration was found to be k1 = 0.9 and b = 0.75 with 5,000 candidates. Therefore, this configuration was reused in all final experiments and no additional hyperparameter tuning was performed. A candidate size of 5,000 was selected as a compromise between retrieval effectiveness and computational cost. Although candidate recall continued to increase beyond 5,000 candidates, ranking metrics such as Recall@10, MRR@10, and nDCG@10 showed little or no improvement. Since BM25 primarily serves as a candidate generator for the subsequent SBERT and BGE-M3 retrieval stages, hyperparameter selection was based mainly on candidate recall. When multiple configurations achieved similar candidate recall values, nDCG@10 was used as a secondary selection criterion.\n",
    "\n",
    "# BGE-M3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "mIiAttOal5XF",
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
    },
    "id": "mIiAttOal5XF",
    "outputId": "2ed0cc5b-5e2b-4ee4-fb1f-9f6694fe564a"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Total 151585 document.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "torch.cuda.empty_cache()\n",
    "gc.collect()\n",
    "\n",
    "candidate_docnos = set(bm25_val_candidates[\"doc_id\"].unique())\n",
    "doc_text_map = {}\n",
    "\n",
    "for doc in corpus_2024.docs_iter():\n",
    "    doc_id = str(doc.doc_id)\n",
    "    if doc_id in candidate_docnos:\n",
    "        title = doc.title if doc.title is not None else \"\"\n",
    "        text = doc.text if doc.text is not None else \"\"\n",
    "        doc_text_map[doc_id] = (title + \" \" + text).strip()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Total {len(doc_text_map)} document.\")"
   ]
  },
